    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="0641" n="553" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg553"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23 Repatriates/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dearing</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-21T12:00:00-05:00">February 21,
                        1933—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Your 93, February 20, 5 p.m., repeated to Legation at Bogotá with
                    instructions to take matter up with the Colombian Government and advise you
                        directly.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d610-f1"/> You may communicate directly with
                    Legation at Bogotá regarding arrangements for repatriation of Colombians.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d610-f1" n="4" xml:id="d610-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 33, February 21, 11 a.m., to the Minister in Colombia, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
